[NAME]
ddccontrol-dbgen \- generate and inspect the ddccontrol CBOR monitor database

[DESCRIPTION]
.B ddccontrol-dbgen
is an offline tool that converts the XML monitor database used by
.BR ddccontrol (1)
into a deterministic CBOR encoding, and validates, dumps, and rewrites
such CBOR databases.
It performs no monitor I/O.

[COMMANDS]
.TP
.B convert
Read the XML database in
.I DIRECTORY
(containing
.I options.xml
and
.IR monitor/*.xml )
and write the CBOR database to
.IR OUTPUT .
.B \-\-revision
overrides the date taken from
.IR options.xml .
.B \-\-snapshot
also writes the snapshot sidecar, which must be installed together
with the CBOR database.
On failure, any existing output and snapshot files are removed.
.TP
.B validate
Check that
.I INPUT
is a valid CBOR database.
.TP
.B dump
Print
.I INPUT
as JSON on standard output.
CBOR maps are written as
.B {"$map": [[key, value], ...]}
and byte strings as
.BR {"$bytes": "hex"} .
.TP
.B rewrite
Re-encode
.I INPUT
to
.IR OUTPUT ,
preserving unknown fields and extensions.

[SEE ALSO]
.BR ddccontrol (1)
.PP
.I /usr/share/doc/ddccontrol-dbgen/README.md
